&lt;p&gt;The Megatron app images are the runtime image plus a &lt;strong&gt;single-step
&lt;code&gt;pip install&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; of a megatron-core wheel built from the
&lt;a href="https://github.com/flagos-ai/Megatron-LM-FL" rel="external" target="_blank"&gt;Megatron-LM-FL&lt;svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;&lt;path fill="currentColor" d="M14 5c-.552 0-1-.448-1-1s.448-1 1-1h6c.552 0 1 .448 1 1v6c0 .552-.448 1-1 1s-1-.448-1-1v-3.586l-7.293 7.293c-.391.39-1.024.39-1.414 0-.391-.391-.391-1.024 0-1.414l7.293-7.293h-3.586zm-9 2c-.552 0-1 .448-1 1v11c0 .552.448 1 1 1h11c.552 0 1-.448 1-1v-4.563c0-.552.448-1 1-1s1 .448 1 1v4.563c0 1.657-1.343 3-3 3h-11c-1.657 0-3-1.343-3-3v-11c0-1.657 1.343-3 3-3h4.563c.552 0 1 .448 1 1s-.448 1-1 1h-4.563z"/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/a&gt; fork. Unlike
vLLM/SGLang — which repack an sdist to strip torch from its dependencies —
megatron is a &lt;strong&gt;fork-source&lt;/strong&gt; path: the wheel keeps its &lt;code&gt;torch&amp;gt;=2.6.0&lt;/code&gt;
requirement and the runtime&amp;rsquo;s vendor torch satisfies it, so pip resolves
nothing and no dependency surgery is needed.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>SGLang</title><link>https://flagos-ai.github.io/release-info/design/sglang/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://flagos-ai.github.io/release-info/design/sglang/</guid><description>&lt;!--
